  "question": "Write a balanced equation for the complete combustion of propane and calculate the mass of carbon dioxide formed from 4.4 g of propane. M(C₃H₈) = 44 g mol⁻¹, M(CO₂) = 44 g mol⁻¹.",
  "supplied_texts": [],
  "response_text": "C₃H₈(g) + 5O₂(g) → 3CO₂(g) + 4H₂O(l)\n\nCheck: C 3 = 3; H 8 = 4 × 2 = 8; O 5 × 2 = 10 = 3 × 2 + 4 = 10.\n\nn(C₃H₈) = 4.4 g ÷ 44 g mol⁻¹ = 0.10 mol\nn(CO₂) = 3 × 0.10 = 0.30 mol\nm(CO₂) = 0.30 × 44 = 13.2 g ≈ 13 g",
  "notation": [
